@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Research
+
+## Request paths
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java`
+  - `GET /private/orders/customers/{id}` currently calls `customerService.getById(id)` and returns HTTP 404 when the customer is absent, before querying orders.
+  - `GET /private/orders` builds an `OrderCriteria` with `page` and `count`, then delegates to `OrderFacade`.
+  - `GET /private/orders/{id}` delegates to `OrderFacade`.
+
+## Causes
+
+1. Orders deliberately store a nullable, scalar `CUSTOMER_ID` in `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/order/Order.java`; there is no JPA relationship to `Customer`. The comment on the field explicitly says an order can survive customer deletion. The delete path in `CustomerServiceImpl` removes customer attributes and the customer, not orders. Therefore order history can be retained, but API code must treat the customer as optional.
+2. `OrderFacadeImpl.getReadableOrder` calls `customerFacade.getCustomerById`. That facade throws `ResourceNotFoundException` when the customer no longer exists, so the method exits before `ReadableOrderPopulator` can expose the persisted billing, delivery, and order email fields. The populator already reads those fields directly from `Order`.
+3. `OrderApi.list(customers/{id})` requires a live `Customer`, so it cannot query the persisted `Order.customerId` after deletion. The existing criteria/repository support filtering by `customerId`, and the response customer object should only be populated when the account still exists.
+4. `OrderRepositoryImpl.listOrders` applies the new page-based pagination through `RepositoryHelper.paginateQuery`. The helper calculates pages as `count / pageSize + 1`, which overcounts exact multiples. More importantly, `OrderFacadeImpl.populateOrderList` creates a new response list but does not copy `totalCount`/`totalPages`; its empty branch always sets `recordsTotal` to 0. Thus a valid later page loses the matching totals, and admin responses do not preserve repository pagination metadata.
+5. `ReadableOrderList` is the API response type and inherits `recordsTotal`/`totalPages` fields from `sm-shop-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/model/entity/ReadableList.java`. `OrderList` inherits `totalCount`/`totalPages` from the core `EntityList`.
+
+## Affected behavior
+
+- Single-order details, order status updates, status history, and payment transactions all use the order id/scalar order data and do not require a live customer, once detail conversion stops treating the optional customer lookup as fatal.
+- Customer-scoped order listing must query by customer id and keep the old account id as the lookup key; it must not query by email. This also preserves separation when a new account is registered with the deleted account's email.
+- Admin filters are assembled in `OrderRepositoryImpl.listOrders`; name/email/id/status filters and newest-first `o.id desc` ordering should remain intact while response totals and page bounds are corrected.
+
+## Files expected to change
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java`
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/utils/RepositoryHelper.java`
+- likely tests under `sm-shop/src/test` and/or `sm-core/src/test` to cover deleted-customer lookup, customer-id order listing, pagination, filters, and empty/out-of-range pages.
